2026-10-19  libtorch-rocm 2.12.0-3

  * pkgver() now reads libtorch/build-version from the extracted archive
    instead of scraping api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/releases/latest.
    The anonymous GitHub API call is rate limited (60 requests/hour) and
    returned an empty string when the limit was hit, aborting every build
    with "pkgver is not allowed to be empty".  Derived from the binary, the
    version can also no longer contradict the sources that source=() pinned
    via the static ${pkgver}.
  * _rocm_ver is pinned to 7.2 instead of probed, and sha256sums are now
    filled in for both sources.  Pinned sums need a fixed artifact, so the
    ROCm auto-probe is gone; bump _rocm_ver together with pkgver and the
    sums.  Note the old probe was broken anyway: _rocm_ver was expanded
    before pkgver was assigned, so every probe URL contained an empty
    version, all probes 404'd, and the package silently fell back to
    rocm7.1 on every system.
  * PyTorch publishes no checksum for libtorch archives (the GitHub release
    only carries pytorch-v2.12.0.tar.gz and torch-2.12.0.tar.gz, and
    <zip>.sha256 is AccessDenied on download.pytorch.org / 404 on the R2
    mirror), so the sums below come from the downloaded archives.
  * Drop curl from makedepends; the only consumer was the removed probe.
  * pkgver() now refuses to relabel: a build-version that disagrees with the
    pinned pkgver is an error instead of being echoed, and a missing file
    falls back to pkgver rather than emitting an empty version.
  * depends gains a rocm-core>=7.2 bound matching the pinned build, so a
    mismatched runtime fails at dependency resolution instead of dlopen()
    with an undefined HIP symbol.

2026-05-23  libtorch-rocm 2.12.0-2

  * Fix ELF load command alignment in pre-built libtorch_cpu.so.
    Upstream PyTorch ROCm binaries ship a zero-length LOAD segment
    with misaligned p_offset, causing glibc's dlopen() to fail with
    "ELF load command address/offset not page-aligned".  The fix
    realigns the segment's p_offset to p_vaddr at build time in
    prepare().  This resolves Audacity's mod-openvino loading failure
    (previously visible as misleading "Inappropriate ioctl for device"
    error due to stale errno reporting).
  * Add python to makedepends for the ELF repair step.
